  29:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c **** #include "arm_math.h"
  30:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c **** 
  31:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c **** /**
  32:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * @ingroup groupFilters
  33:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  */
  34:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c **** 
  35:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c **** /**
  36:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * @defgroup LMS Least Mean Square (LMS) Filters
  37:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  *
  38:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * LMS filters are a class of adaptive filters that are able to "learn" an unknown transfer functio
  39:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * LMS filters use a gradient descent method in which the filter coefficients are updated based on 
  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * Adaptive filters are often used in communication systems, equalizers, and noise removal.
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * The CMSIS DSP Library contains LMS filter functions that operate on Q15, Q31, and floating-point
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * The library also contains normalized LMS filters in which the filter coefficient adaptation is i
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  *
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * An LMS filter consists of two components as shown below.
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * The first component is a standard transversal or FIR filter.
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * The second component is a coefficient update mechanism.
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * The LMS filter has two input signals.
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * The "input" feeds the FIR filter while the "reference input" corresponds to the desired output o
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * That is, the FIR filter coefficients are updated so that the output of the FIR filter matches th
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * The filter coefficient update mechanism is based on the difference between the FIR filter output
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * This "error signal" tends towards zero as the filter adapts.
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * The LMS processing functions accept the input and reference input signals and generate the filte
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * \image html LMS.gif "Internal structure of the Least Mean Square filter"
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  *
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * The functions operate on blocks of data and each call to the function processes
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * <code>blockSize</code> samples through the filter.
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * <code>pSrc</code> points to input signal, <code>pRef</code> points to reference signal,
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * <code>pOut</code> points to output signal and <code>pErr</code> points to error signal.
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * All arrays contain <code>blockSize</code> values.
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  *
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * The functions operate on a block-by-block basis.
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * Internally, the filter coefficients <code>b[n]</code> are updated on a sample-by-sample basis.
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * The convergence of the LMS filter is slower compared to the normalized LMS algorithm.
  64:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  *
  65:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * \par Algorithm:
  66:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * The output signal <code>y[n]</code> is computed by a standard FIR filter:
  67:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * <pre>
  68:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  *     y[n] = b[0] * x[n] + b[1] * x[n-1] + b[2] * x[n-2] + ...+ b[numTaps-1] * x[n-numTaps+1]
  69:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * </pre>
  70:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  *
  71:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * \par
  72:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * The error signal equals the difference between the reference signal <code>d[n]</code> and the fi
  73:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * <pre>
  74:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  *     e[n] = d[n] - y[n].
  75:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * </pre>
  76:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  *
  77:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * \par
  78:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * After each sample of the error signal is computed, the filter coefficients <code>b[k]</code> are
  79:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * <pre>
  80:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  *     b[k] = b[k] + e[n] * mu * x[n-k],  for k=0, 1, ..., numTaps-1
  81:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * </pre>
  82:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * where <code>mu</code> is the step size and controls the rate of coefficient convergence.
  83:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  *\par
  84:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * In the APIs, <code>pCoeffs</code> points to a coefficient array of size <code>numTaps</code>.
  85:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * Coefficients are stored in time reversed order.
ARM GAS  C:\Users\Lamp\AppData\Local\Temp\ccDBksd1.s 			page 3


  86:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * \par
  87:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * <pre>
  88:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  *    {b[numTaps-1], b[numTaps-2], b[N-2], ..., b[1], b[0]}
  89:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * </pre>
  90:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * \par
  91:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * <code>pState</code> points to a state array of size <code>numTaps + blockSize - 1</code>.
  92:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * Samples in the state buffer are stored in the order:
  93:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * \par
  94:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * <pre>
  95:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  *    {x[n-numTaps+1], x[n-numTaps], x[n-numTaps-1], x[n-numTaps-2]....x[0], x[1], ..., x[blockSize
  96:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * </pre>
  97:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * \par
  98:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * Note that the length of the state buffer exceeds the length of the coefficient array by <code>bl
  99:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * The increased state buffer length allows circular addressing, which is traditionally used in FIR
 100:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * to be avoided and yields a significant speed improvement.
 101:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * The state variables are updated after each block of data is processed.
 102:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * \par Instance Structure
 103:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * The coefficients and state variables for a filter are stored together in an instance data struct
 104:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * A separate instance structure must be defined for each filter and
 105:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * coefficient and state arrays cannot be shared among instances.
 106:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * There are separate instance structure declarations for each of the 3 supported data types.
 107:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  *
 108:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * \par Initialization Functions
 109:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * There is also an associated initialization function for each data type.
 110:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * The initialization function performs the following operations:
 111:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * - Sets the values of the internal structure fields.
 112:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * - Zeros out the values in the state buffer.
 113:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * To do this manually without calling the init function, assign the follow subfields of the instan
 114:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * numTaps, pCoeffs, mu, postShift (not for f32), pState. Also set all of the values in pState to z
 115:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  *
 116:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * \par
 117:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * Use of the initialization function is optional.
 118:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * However, if the initialization function is used, then the instance structure cannot be placed in
 119:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * To place an instance structure into a const data section, the instance structure must be manuall
 120:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * Set the values in the state buffer to zeros before static initialization.
 121:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * The code below statically initializes each of the 3 different data type filter instance structur
 122:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * <pre>
 123:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  *    arm_lms_instance_f32 S = {numTaps, pState, pCoeffs, mu};
 124:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  *    arm_lms_instance_q31 S = {numTaps, pState, pCoeffs, mu, postShift};
 125:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  *    arm_lms_instance_q15 S = {numTaps, pState, pCoeffs, mu, postShift};
 126:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * </pre>
 127:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * where <code>numTaps</code> is the number of filter coefficients in the filter; <code>pState</cod
 128:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * <code>pCoeffs</code> is the address of the coefficient buffer; <code>mu</code> is the step size 
 129:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  *
 130:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * \par Fixed-Point Behavior:
 131:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * Care must be taken when using the Q15 and Q31 versions of the LMS filter.
 132:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * The following issues must be considered:
 133:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * - Scaling of coefficients
 134:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * - Overflow and saturation
 135:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  *
 136:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * \par Scaling of Coefficients:
 137:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * Filter coefficients are represented as fractional values and
 138:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * coefficients are restricted to lie in the range <code>[-1 +1)</code>.
 139:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * The fixed-point functions have an additional scaling parameter <code>postShift</code>.
 140:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * At the output of the filter's accumulator is a shift register which shifts the result by <code>p
 141:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * This essentially scales the filter coefficients by <code>2^postShift</code> and
 142:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * allows the filter coefficients to exceed the range <code>[+1 -1)</code>.
ARM GAS  C:\Users\Lamp\AppData\Local\Temp\ccDBksd1.s 			page 4


 143:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * The value of <code>postShift</code> is set by the user based on the expected gain through the sy
 144:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  *
 145:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * \par Overflow and Saturation:
 146:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * Overflow and saturation behavior of the fixed-point Q15 and Q31 versions are
 147:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * described separately as part of the function specific documentation below.
 148:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  */
 149:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c **** 
 150:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c **** /**
 151:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * @addtogroup LMS
 152:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * @{
 153:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  */
 154:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c **** 
 155:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c **** /**
 156:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * @details
 157:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * This function operates on floating-point data types.
 158:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  *
 159:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * @brief Processing function for floating-point LMS filter.
 160:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * @param[in]  *S points to an instance of the floating-point LMS filter structure.
 161:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * @param[in]  *pSrc points to the block of input data.
 162:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * @param[in]  *pRef points to the block of reference data.
 163:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * @param[out] *pOut points to the block of output data.
 164:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * @param[out] *pErr points to the block of error data.
 165:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * @param[in]  blockSize number of samples to process.
 166:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  * @return     none.
 167:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****  */
 168:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c **** 
 169:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c **** void arm_lms_f32(
 170:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****   const arm_lms_instance_f32 * S,
 171:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****   float32_t * pSrc,
 172:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****   float32_t * pRef,
 173:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****   float32_t * pOut,
 174:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****   float32_t * pErr,
 175:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c ****   uint32_t blockSize)
 176:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_lms_f32.c **** {
  31              		.loc 1 176 1 view -0
